{"tool_name":"muddy_db","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"muddy_db","home":"https://muddy-db.shinyapps.io/muddy_db/","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Biologically-oriented mud volcano database.","addition_date":"2022-05-19T22:46:11.648163Z","last_update_date":"2022-05-19T22:46:11.650659Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Database portal"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:muddy_db","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"rahela.carpa@ubbcluj.ro","name":"Rahela Carpa","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Alexei Remizovschi"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Aggregation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3436"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"muddy_db","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.7717/PEERJ.12463","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 Copyright 2021 Remizovschi and CarpaMud volcanoes (MVs) are naturally occurring hydrocarbon hotbeds with continuous methane discharge, contributing to global warming. They host microbial communities adapted to hydrocarbon oxidation. Given their research value, MVs still represent a niche topic in microbiology and are neglected by hydrocarbon-oriented research. All the data regarding MVs is sporadic and decentralized. To mitigate this problem, we built a custom Natural Language Processing pipeline (muddy_mine), and collected all the available MV data from open-access articles. Based on this data, we built the muddy_db database. The muddy_db represents the first biologically oriented database rendered as a user-friendly web app. This database includes all the relevant MV data, ranging from microbial taxonomy to hydrocarbon occurrence and geology. The muddy_mine and muddy_db tools are licensed under the GPLv3. muddy_db R Shiny web app: https://muddy-db.shinyapps.io/muddy_db/muddy_db R package: https://github.com/TracyRage/m